<!--
    kuna-dynalloca: a variable-length array moves the stack pointer by a
    run-time amount (option dynalloca).

    Source (gcc -O2, x86-64):
      int vla(int n) { char buf[n]; return use(buf, n); }
      movslq %edi,%rax ; add $0xf,%rax ; and $-16,%rax ; sub %rax,%rsp ; mov %rsp,%rdi ; call use

    Stage: P7, RuleDynAlloca: PTRADD(stack pointer, -n, 1) with n not a
    constant becomes alloca(n) (Hex-Rays prints alloca for sub rsp, reg).

    Pass 1 (default) prints alloca(...); pass 2 (dynalloca off) the stack
    pointer arithmetic.
-->
